let _embed_updates_md : String =
  #|# Update rendering and preservation
  #|
  #|`update` uses the same parser, execution, comparisons, and failure reports as
  #|`test`.
  #|
  #|## Before previewing or applying an update
  #|
  #|- **Dry-run still executes code.** `update` and `update --dry-run` build and run
  #|  programs with your permissions, without a sandbox or temporary workspace
  #|  isolation. Dry-run leaves Markdown unchanged; programs can still modify files.
  #|- **Passing cases are included.** Every successfully executed case is rendered.
  #|  Expectations and fences may be normalized even when the assertions passed;
  #|  review the full document diff, not only the failing case.
  #|- **Execution errors block the entire document's update.** A build, timeout,
  #|  target-resolution or other execution error prevents all expectation edits and
  #|  dry-run document diffs for that document. Other documents can still update;
  #|  earlier updates and program effects are not rolled back.
  #|- **Update success does not mean assertions passed.** `update --dry-run` can
  #|  print `FAIL` and exit with `0` when it completes without errors. Use `test`
  #|  for the CI pass/fail decision. Mooncram's status is independent of the tested
  #|  program's expected `[N]` status.
  #|
  #|For an intentional behavior change, preview, review, apply, then verify:
  #|
  #|```sh
  #|mooncram update tests/example.md --dry-run
  #|mooncram update tests/example.md
  #|mooncram test tests/example.md
  #|```
  #|
  #|Replace `tests/example.md` with your input. Keep any nondefault `--target` and
  #|`--timeout-ms` options the same on all three commands. Fix unintended behavior
  #|in the program before updating expectations.
  #|
  #|## What an update changes
  #|
  #|A document is written or shown as a dry-run diff only when its bytes change.
  #|With unchanged program output and exit status, repeating an update leaves the
  #|file unchanged and reports `updated 0`.
  #|
  #|Updates preserve glob/regex patterns that still match the corresponding output.
  #|New or changed output without a retained matching pattern becomes an exact
  #|expectation; expectations for removed output disappear. Exact expectations may
  #|be normalized, including redundant `(escaped)` spellings, even when a case
  #|already passes. `(no-eol)` reflects the actual stream's final newline.
  #|
  #|Ordinary output is written directly. JSON strings with `(escaped)` protect
  #|control characters and output that could be read as a command, `#cwd` declaration,
  #|stream marker, annotation, or final exit-status marker. Empty output produces no
  #|output lines; significant blank output lines use `"" (escaped)` where needed.
  #|Zero exit statuses are omitted even when originally explicit; nonzero statuses
  #|use canonical `[N]` spelling.
  #|
  #|All cases in a fence share the shortest safe opening/closing backtick length,
  #|with a minimum of three. Fences may grow to contain output resembling a closing
  #|fence, or shrink when unnecessarily long, including for passing cases.
  #|
  #|Only expectation text and fence markers change. Commands, block configuration,
  #|surrounding prose, separator lines, and text outside edited spans stay intact,
  #|including a missing final document newline. Existing output rows retain their
  #|Markdown container prefixes and newline style where possible; new output follows
  #|the command's layout. Indentation may be adjusted so output spaces survive
  #|Markdown parsing.
  #|
  #|Paired cases retain marker order, leading and section separator blanks,
  #|`(ignore)`, and satisfied `(empty)` constraints. A violated `(empty)` becomes a
  #|plain marker with rendered output. Each stream is updated independently.
  #|
  #|Before writing or showing a diff, mooncram validates that the updated document
  #|preserves its cases, commands, and configuration and matches the captured results.
  #|Validation failure cancels the entire document update. Each changed case
  #|counts once, including pure normalization; changing shared fence markers counts
  #|every case in that fence.
  #|
  #|In dry-run mode, each document with eligible edits additionally prints:
  #|
  #|```text
  #|--- <canonical-file>
  #|+++ <canonical-file> (updated)
  #|<document diff hunks>
  #|```
  #|
  #|This is in addition to individual failure reports. A proposed diff describes
  #|eligible document edits; the final `test` verifies that the updated cases pass.
  #|

///|
pub let updates_md : String = _embed_updates_md
